D.bOA=new A.LP("Safety first","\ud83e\uddba",B.cr,D.d2J)
D.bOp=new A.jw("Wire colours","Black is hot (it carries the power), white is neutral (the way back), bare copper or green is ground (the safety path). Red is a second hot, often used for a switched line.")
D.bOw=new A.jw("Screw colours","On an outlet the brass screw takes the hot wire, the silver screw takes the neutral and the green screw takes the ground.")
D.bOj=new A.jw("Wire size","14 gauge wire is for 15 amp circuits (lights and outlets). 12 gauge is for 20 amp circuits (kitchens). A thinner wire than the breaker allows can overheat and start a fire.")
D.bOd=new A.jw("Breakers","A breaker is a safety switch. It trips when a circuit carries too much current, so the wires never get hot enough to burn.")
D.bOr=new A.jw("Wire nuts","Strip about 3/4 inch, twist the bare ends together clockwise, and screw on the nut until no bare copper shows. Give each wire a gentle tug.")
D.bOx=new A.jw("Switches","A switch cuts the hot wire only. The neutral goes straight through to the light.")
D.bOy=new A.jw("GFCI","A GFCI outlet watches the current going out and coming back. If a little leaks (through water or a person) it cuts the power in a fraction of a second.")
D.bO6=new A.jw("Ceiling fans","A fan shakes and is heavy. It needs a box that says fan rated, fixed to the joist, not a plain light box.")
D.bO8=new A.jw("Heights","Outlets sit about 16 inches from the floor. Switches sit about 48 inches up, where your hand falls.")
D.cWJ=w([D.bOp,D.bOw,D.bOj,D.bOd,D.bOr,D.bOx,D.bOy,D.bO6,D.bO8],x.Z)
