D.bO5=new A.jw("Hot left, cold right","On a faucet, hot is on the left and cold on the right. Hot lines are marked red and cold lines blue.")
D.bOi=new A.jw("The P-trap","The curved pipe under a sink always holds a little water. That water seal stops sewer gas coming up the drain.")
D.bOt=new A.jw("Shut-off valves","Every sink and toilet has its own small valve, so you can stop the water to one fixture without turning off the whole house.")
D.bOb=new A.jw("Slip nuts","Drain joints are sealed by a washer and a slip nut. Tighten by hand and a quarter turn: too much force cracks plastic.")
D.bOa=new A.jw("Wax ring","A toilet sits on a wax ring that seals it to the floor drain. A toilet is lowered straight down once, and cannot be slid around.")
D.bOq=new A.jw("Drain slope","Drains fall about 1/4 inch per foot so water and waste keep moving. Too flat and it clogs, too steep and the water leaves the solids behind.")
D.bOv=new A.jw("Order of work","Plumbing goes from the top down on the drain (tailpiece, trap, arm) and from the wall out on the supply (valve, hose, fixture).")
D.c51=w([D.bO5,D.bOi,D.bOt,D.bOb,D.bOa,D.bOq,D.bOv],x.Z)
D.bOB=new A.LP("Plumbing basics","\ud83d\udeb0",B.cu,D.c51)
D.bO7=new A.jw("Studs","Studs are the vertical 2x4 posts inside a wall, 16 inches apart from centre to centre. Everything is fixed to them.")
D.bOl=new A.jw("Drilling studs","Holes for cable go through the middle of the stud, so a nail or screw cannot reach the wire.")
D.bOc=new A.jw("Drywall","A sheet is 4 feet wide, so its edges land on studs 48 inches apart. Screws go into studs only, just under the paper.")
D.bOf=new A.jw("Taping and mud","Seams get paper tape and three thin coats of joint compound, sanded smooth between coats, then primer and paint.")
D.bOu=new A.jw("Order of a build","Frame, run the pipes and wires (rough-in), inspect, hang drywall, finish it, paint, then fit the fixtures and devices.")
D.cIX=w([D.bO7,D.bOl,D.bOc,D.bOf,D.bOu],x.Z)
D.bOz=new A.LP("Framing and walls","\ud83c\udfe0",B.dU,D.cIX)
D.bOg=new A.jw("Voltage tester","A pen that glows or beeps near live wires. Test it on a known live outlet first, so you know it works.")
D.bOm=new A.jw("Wire strippers","Strip the plastic off without nicking the copper. A nick weakens the wire.")
D.bOs=new A.jw("Adjustable wrench","For nuts on valves and hoses. Hold the fitting steady with a second wrench so you do not twist the pipe.")
D.bOk=new A.jw("Drill and screw gun","A drill makes holes through studs. A screw gun sets drywall screws to the right depth.")
D.bOe=new A.jw("Level and tape measure","Measure twice, cut once. A level makes sure outlets, shelves and pipes are straight.")
